{
  "$comment": [
    "Mandated Services Registry — the one allow-list for `webfetch`.",
    "",
    "Enforcement: OpenCode 1.18.30 types `webfetch` as Action only (ask|allow|deny),",
    "so a config domain map is impossible. The list is enforced by a plugin guard",
    "(adapters/opencode/plugins/agent-tooling.js -> policies/webfetch_mandated.py):",
    "a host not listed here is DENIED with an explicit-request message. The config",
    "keeps `webfetch: \"ask\"`, so a mandated host still prompts — webfetch remains the",
    "last resort, and a plugin load failure degrades to a prompt rather than to open.",
    "",
    "Derivation: the `kind: connector` entries are validated against the connector",
    "library tables in agent-tooling/skills/source-connectors/SKILL.md by",
    "scripts/mandated_services.py. Add a connector row there and the drift check fails",
    "until this file is updated; remove one and it fails the other way. The remaining",
    "entries are Wikimedia data APIs, compute (LiftWing), and docs/tool hosts, each",
    "naming the skill or script that documents it. A host that is part of a service but",
    "not in the library's endpoint column (Flickr's image CDN) is declared under",
    "`auxiliary_hosts`, which is allowed but not drift-checked.",
    "",
    "Known gap (stated, not hidden): this gates the `webfetch` door only. Python and",
    "shell scripts reach the network directly (`llm_provider.py`, `source_discovery.py`,",
    "the bench suite), and no OS control covers the network. `websearch` is a separate,",
    "provider-mediated door (not URL-addressable) and is not covered here either. The",
    "guard also judges only the requested host: a mandated host that redirects to an",
    "unlisted one is not re-checked (tool.execute.before cannot see the redirect target).",
    "The registry is a webfetch boundary, not a network chokepoint.",
    "",
    "Hosts are matched case-insensitively, exact first, then `host_suffixes` (a leading",
    "dot matches the apex and any subdomain: `.wikipedia.org` matches wikipedia.org,",
    "en.wikipedia.org, but never notwikipedia.org). IP literals and localhost are never",
    "mandated. No secrets, no machine identity: safe for the public repo."
  ],

